    "rationale": "Evidence from iteration 3 (score 159.2, the best so far, kp 2.5, sensor_size 0.016, base_speed 1.3, kd 0.3, weights [2,1,0,-1,-2], last_direction). Every run still ended off_track. max_error was 0.0606 on the oval, 0.0623 on the s-bend and 0.0616 on the slalom, against the 0.06 m limit. line_loss_events were 1.25, 2.0 and 1.0. steering_oscillation was 0.28, 0.20 and 0.14, which is low. The only finish was one oval run at 1.89 s, so speed is adequate there.\n\nThe kp lever has stopped helping. Raising kp from 2.0 to 2.5 improved the oval max_error (0.0624 to 0.0606) and slalom (0.0622 to 0.0616), but worsened the s-bend (0.0616 to 0.0623) and raised s-bend line losses (1.15 to 2.0). That pattern suggests overshoot on the bend rather than too little steering authority. Evaluator rule (c) would push kp to 3.0, which I expect to worsen that overshoot. Rule (d), switching line_loss to search_right, is also unlikely to help: search_right steers left regardless of which side the line is on, while last_direction steers back toward the side where the line was last seen.\n\nI therefore change one field: controller.kd from 0.3 to 0.5. Oscillation is low (0.14 to 0.28), so there is damping headroom, and the derivative term should curb the overshoot that is pushing the s-bend and slalom over the edge. kp 2.5, sensor_size 0.016, base_speed 1.3, ki 0.05, weights and last_direction stay unchanged to isolate the effect.\n\nExpected result: s-bend line_loss_events fall toward 1 or below, max_error drops under about 0.059 m on at least two tracks, and steering_oscillation stays under about 0.35. Hypotheses for next steps: (1) if max_error stays at or above 0.06 with kd 0.5 and oscillation still low, reduce base_speed to about 1.1 to test whether corner speed is causing the excursions (the oval finish time leaves margin). (2) If line loss stays at 1 or more with kd 0.5, test line_loss = search_right as the only change. (3) If oscillation rises sharply above about 0.4,